  ✓ Checkout Sessions (Recommended)
  ✓ Payment Intents
  ✗ Payment Intents with setup_future_usage
  ✗ Setup Intents
  ✗ Off-session payments

1. Only supports send_invoice collection method.
### Invoices 

Invoices using SeQura only support the [`send_invoice`](https://docs.stripe.com/api/invoices/object.md#invoice_object-collection_method) collection method.

### Payment line items 

SeQura uses the contents of the shopper’s cart in its risk assessment. Send [payment line items](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-line-items.md) with every SeQura payment so that SeQura receives the product name, product code, unit cost, quantity, tax, and discount for each item.

- **Checkout:** Stripe automatically sends the line items from your Checkout Session.
- **Payment Intents API:** Pass `amount_details[line_items]` when you create or update the PaymentIntent. Without it, SeQura receives only the total amount.

## Connect 

| Capability | Requirement |
| --- | --- |
| `sequra_payments` | Connected accounts must have this capability enabled. Request it during account creation or by updating an existing connected account. |

If you use Connect, you must consider the following before you enable SeQura on connected accounts. To accept SeQura payments, connected accounts must have the sequra_payments capability enabled. You can request this capability during account creation or update an existing connected account. How you structure the charge also matters: with direct charges, the connected account is the merchant of record and their statement descriptor appears on the customer’s bank statement. With destination charges or transfer charges, your platform is the merchant of record. Review the Connect documentation for guidance on charge types and how they interact with payment method capabilities.

## Customer experience 

#### 1. Select payment method

The customer selects SeQura at checkout.

#### 2. Create or log in

On both desktop and mobile, the customer is redirected from your website or app to SeQura's hosted payment page. The payment flow is the same on every device.

#### 3. Accept terms

The customer chooses a repayment option and completes payment authorization on SeQura's hosted page within 60 minutes. If they don't, the payment attempt expires and the PaymentIntent returns to requires_payment_method.

#### 4. Payment Complete

The customer sees a SeQura confirmation screen, then returns to your website or app.

### Transaction identifiers 

Payments made with SeQura appear on the buyer’s statement as SeQura rather than your Stripe statement descriptor. For Connect scenarios, learn more about how [statement descriptors are set with Connect](https://docs.stripe.com/connect/statement-descriptors.md). After a payment completes, expand `latest_charge` on the PaymentIntent to retrieve the SeQura transaction ID from `latest_charge.payment_method_details.sequra.transaction_id`. Share it with customers to help them locate the payment when contacting SeQura support.

## Enable SeQura 

If you use Stripe front-end products, enable SeQura in your [payment method settings](https://dashboard.stripe.com/settings/payment_methods). Stripe automatically determines which payment methods are most relevant to each customer.

If your integration requires manually listing payment methods, you can [configure SeQura as an accepted payment method](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/sequra/accept-a-payment.md).
